  "narrative": {
    "intro": "CACI Federal obligated $2.4B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date across 201 awards, with an average award size of $11.9M. Obligations are down 32.1% year over year. Annual obligations rose from $1.3B in FY21 to $3.5B in FY25 before falling to $2.4B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.3B, followed by the General Services Administration at $797M and the Department of Homeland Security at $169M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $988M, followed by Engineering Services at $564M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $195M. Smaller markets include Landscape Architectural Services at $12.5M and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $9.4M. Current-year totals are partial, and award-value figures in tables are total contract values rather than obligations.",
